{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792752054,"nonce":"iwH/uULQx3giATd4hasf7DXxAnY=","title":"Preserve runtime types when editor macro expansion fails","message":"A macro declaration's Expr/ExprOf\u003cT\u003e annotations describe compiler transport. Unexpanded macro calls currently expose these as runtime signatures, producing expected Expr found String, ExprOf return hovers, or aborting the body and losing later local identities when expansion fails.\n\nReproduced an unavailable dependency macro with ExprOf\u003cSheet\u003e: the failure is reported but the call's hover is absent. Preserve the actual macro error, project ExprOf\u003cT\u003e to T and Expr to unknown for the editor's runtime call view, and continue typing the rest of the body. Production compilation must retain its failure behavior. Verify CompiledCss.file and Hxx.hxx without per-library special cases.","files":null}]}